        "Urgent danger, medical need, child safety, evidence at risk, and ongoing threats deserve immediate action. But sending the same packet twenty times in a day may make it harder to identify your latest material. Create a short urgent cover note, identify the specific risk, dispatch through an appropriate official route, and consult counsel. For non-emergency follow-up, keep a dispatch log and proceed through the escalation ladder deliberately.",
