        "A typo, missing date, or later-discovered document does not require a new fictional version of the story. Preserve the original, prepare a dated correction or supplement, and explain what changed. If you are unsure whether an issue is material, show both versions to counsel. A transparent correction demonstrates care; a secret replacement can look like an attempt to manipulate the record.",
        "This applies to witness information as well. Record what each person personally knows and do not ask multiple people to sign identical language drafted for them. Genuine differences in memory are normal. Coaching facts or coordinating statements can harm both safety and credibility.",
